========================== Q12 ==============================

Will this compile?

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int x = 10;

        Runnable r = () -> {
            x++;
            System.out.println(x);
        };

        r.run();
    }
}

ANSWER:
NO — Compile-time error.

Reason:
A local variable captured by a lambda must be
final or effectively final.

x++ modifies x.


