========================== Q28 ==============================

Find the problem.

interface A {
    void show();
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        A a = () -> {
            System.out.println("Hello");
            System.out.println("World");
            return 10;
        };

        a.show();
    }
}

ANSWER:

NO — Compile-time error.

Reason:

show() returns void.

But the lambda tries to return:

return 10;

A void-compatible lambda cannot return a value.

Correct:

A a = () -> {
    System.out.println("Hello");
    System.out.println("World");
};

